# Chroma library, modern Earth: THE SPHERES OF SOCIETY, title moments of sphere titles set c. Library thread,
# 2026-10-09, "v22" update stage 4, item 15 (chroma-packs/spheres/title-gaps.md, "The 28 new titles").
# An everyday pair per new title of titles.py that only its holder meets (holds:), in the style of
# earth-titles-careers.lib: the first or second moment grows from the title's turning point, the other is a later
# stretch of the same post.
# Syntax: header of build.py. Rules: SPEC.md. Every moment carries sphere: <sphere>, every option the face it acts in
# (a cross option X>Y the means colour's face). ladder: is the rung the title sits on in that face's ladder
# (character.jobs, read rung by rung); haunt: where the work is done at a haunt among its regulars.
# Evenness: every one-colour option has chance 75 and every cross option 65, so each colour's mean is the same.
# Pairs (complementary calls; cross cycles s1 and s2 four times each, s3 and s4 three times each):
#   physiotherapist     BR (s1) / WUG (s2)    hospice volunteer   RG (s3) / WUB (s4)
#   teaching assistant  WU (s1) / BRG (s2)    consultant          UB (s3) / WRG (s4)
#   mechanic            UR (s1) / WBG (s2)    language teacher    GU (s3) / WBR (s4)
#   outdoor instructor  WG (s1) / UBR (s2)
# Children: in the teaching assistant's and the outdoor instructor's moments every option keeps the children safe;
# none takes a child into danger.
# holds: names the new titles, which are not yet in earth_perks_titles.py (they wait for NEW_TITLES to be merged).

# ================================================================ physiotherapist (care.B)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls BR (cycle s1); partner: six sessions to climb the stairs

== signed fit for the cup final
tier: everyday
sphere: care
ladder: known
at: employer
rate: 0.5
share: .0015
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 22-70
calls: BR
holds: physiotherapist
tone: trouble
life: work
horizon: week
roles: boss, a patient
earth: a semi-professional player asks you to sign him fit for the cup final, and his knee is two weeks from ready
times: Most physiotherapists who treat sport, a few times in their working years; players and clubs pressing for a return before the body is healed is a common strain of sports physiotherapy (estimate)
gap: 1-3
scene: A semi-professional player from the town club wants {N} to sign him fit for Saturday's cup final. His knee is two weeks from ready, and the club pays {Ns} invoices.
scene W: The form asks for an honest word on whether the knee will hold. It is the same form for a cup final as for a Tuesday.
scene U: {N} has the measurements: the knee bends ten degrees short, and the hop test is weak on that side.
scene B: The club's manager sends {N} half of the practice's patients. A club that hears no once may find another physiotherapist.
scene R: The player is twenty-four and has waited all his life for a final. {N} can feel how badly he wants it.
scene G: The body mends at its own pace, and a knee pushed now may not be the same at forty.
- W | write exactly what the tests show on the club's form | v: conformity, universalism | sphere: care.W | chance: 75
- U | run the tests again in front of him, and let the numbers speak | v: achievement, universalism | sphere: care.U | chance: 75
- B | sign him fit with a strapping, and keep the club's custom | v: security, power | closed: approval: signing a patient fit who is not; backfire: the knee goes in the final | sphere: care.B | chance: 75
- R | tell him straight he could lose the knee for good, and see what he says | v: self-direction, benevolence | sphere: care.R | chance: 75
- G | tell him to let the knee heal in its own time and come back next season | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: care.G | chance: 75
- W>U | go by the published return-to-play steps, one test at a time | v: conformity, achievement | sphere: care.W | chance: 65
- U>B | show the manager the injury figures, and sell the club a proper recovery plan | v: achievement, power | sphere: care.U | chance: 65
- B>R | agree to twenty minutes off the bench, on your own terms and in writing | act: agree to twenty minutes off the bench, on their own terms and in writing | v: power, stimulation | sphere: care.B | chance: 65
- R>G | sit through the final on the bench beside him, with ice and a cool head | v: benevolence | sphere: care.R | chance: 65
- G>W | ask the club's old captain to tell the team why he must sit this one out | v: tradition, conformity | sphere: care.G | chance: 65
works: The player sits out the final, cheers from the bench, and plays the whole of the next season.
works: The manager grumbles for a week, then sends {N} the rest of the squad.
fails: The club finds a physiotherapist who will sign the form, and the invoices stop.
fails: The knee holds for an hour of the final, then gives way, and the town talks of little else.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls WUG (cycle s2); partner: signed fit for the cup final

== six sessions to climb the stairs
tier: everyday
sphere: care
haunt: care.houses
ladder: known
at: hospital
rate: 0.5
share: .0015
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 22-70
calls: WUG
holds: physiotherapist
tone: mixed
life: work
horizon: week
roles: boss, colleague
earth: the ward allows six sessions after a mended hip, and an old woman needs more than six to manage the stairs at home
times: Most hospital physiotherapists, several times a year; a set number of sessions that some older patients outrun is a routine strain of ward work (estimate)
gap: 0.5-1
scene: An old woman of eighty-one has had her hip mended and wants to go home to her narrow house with its steep stairs. The ward allows six sessions with {N}. On the sixth she still cannot manage the stairs alone.
scene W: Six sessions is the rule for every hip on the ward, so the waiting list moves for everyone.
scene U: {N} has charted each session: two more steps each day. At that rate she needs four more.
scene B: {boss} judges the team by how fast the beds clear. A patient kept on costs the ward a bed.
scene R: She grips the rail and swears at the stairs, laughing. {N} likes her enormously.
scene G: Her son lives two streets away, and the neighbours already take turns with her shopping.
- W | discharge her on the sixth session, as the rule says, with an exercise sheet | v: conformity, security | sphere: care.W | chance: 75
- U | write up her chart and ask for four more sessions on the evidence | v: achievement, universalism | lever: voice | sphere: care.U | chance: 75
- B | offer her private evenings at your own clinic, at a fee her son can pay | act: offer her private evenings at their own clinic, at a fee her son can pay | v: achievement, power | sphere: care.B | chance: 75
- R | squeeze her in at lunch every day this week, off the books | v: benevolence, stimulation | sphere: care.R | chance: 75
- G | teach her son and a neighbour to walk her up the stairs each evening | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: care.G | chance: 75
- W>B | apply by the book for a stair rail at home, so she pays nothing | v: security, conformity | sphere: care.W | chance: 65
- U>R | work out a stair drill for her own back step, and free her from the ward | v: self-direction, achievement | sphere: care.U | chance: 65
- B>G | call in a favour with the community team to visit her at home | v: power, benevolence | sphere: care.B | chance: 65
- R>W | stand up at the team meeting and say six sessions fail the oldest patients | v: universalism | lever: voice | sphere: care.R | chance: 65
- G>U | ask her family to measure every step at home, and practise on those | v: benevolence, achievement | sphere: care.G | chance: 65
works: She goes home a week later and climbs her own stairs to bed that night.
works: {boss} reads {Ns} chart and adds two sessions for every patient over eighty.
fails: She goes home on time, and her bed ends up in the front room downstairs.
fails: {boss} notes the extra hours, and {N} is moved to the outpatient list.

# ================================================================ hospice volunteer (care.G)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls RG (cycle s3); partner: a letter to a daughter twenty years gone

== the old dog at the hospice window
tier: everyday
sphere: care
haunt: care.houses
ladder: regular
at: charity
rate: 0.5
share: .008
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 16-90
calls: RG
holds: hospice volunteer
tone: mixed
life: community
horizon: week
roles: colleague, neighbour
earth: a dying woman asks you to bring her old dog to see her, and dogs are not allowed on the ward
times: Many hospice volunteers, once in their years on the rota; a last visit from a pet is a familiar wish in hospice care (estimate)
gap: 1-3
scene: On {Ns} Thursday shift at the hospice, an old woman in the end room asks for one thing: to see her dog. He is staying with a neighbour across town, and dogs are not allowed on the ward.
scene W: The rule keeps the ward clean for every patient. It was not written with one last visit in mind.
scene U: {N} has read that some hospices let animals in on a careful plan: one room, one hour, the nurse told first.
scene B: The volunteer coordinator decides who gets the good shifts, and does not like surprises.
scene R: She has days, maybe less. {N} wants that dog on her bed by tonight.
scene G: She talks about him the way people talk about family. He has slept at the foot of her bed for twelve years.
- W | ask the nurse in charge, properly, whether an exception can be made | v: conformity, benevolence | sphere: care.W | chance: 75
- U | find a hospice that allows pet visits, and bring the nurse in charge its rules | v: universalism, benevolence | lever: voice | sphere: care.U | chance: 75
- B | tell her family how to ask for the visit, and keep your name out of it | act: tell her family how to ask for the visit, and keep their name out of it | v: security | sphere: care.B | chance: 75
- R | fetch the dog in your own car and walk him in by the side door | act: fetch the dog in their own car and walk him in by the side door | v: benevolence, stimulation | sphere: care.R | chance: 75
- G | wheel her bed to the garden window, and have the dog brought to the lawn | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: care.G | chance: 75
- W>R | get the visit signed off by the nurse, then give her the whole afternoon with him | v: benevolence, hedonism | sphere: care.W | chance: 65
- U>G | find the room that opens straight onto the garden, and plan the visit there | v: benevolence | sphere: care.U | chance: 65
- B>W | offer to cover the coordinator's weekend if the ward writes a rule for pet visits | v: power, universalism | sphere: care.B | chance: 65
- R>U | ring round the vets in town until one explains how to make the visit safe | v: stimulation, universalism | sphere: care.R | chance: 65
- G>B | ask her family whether she would rather go home for a day to see him | v: self-direction, tradition | sphere: care.G | chance: 65
works: The dog climbs onto the bed and goes to sleep against her, and the whole ward hears her laugh.
works: The hospice writes a rule for pet visits that spring, and the other volunteers thank {N} for it.
fails: The coordinator says no, and the woman dies before the neighbour can bring the dog to the window.
fails: The visit happens, and {N} is taken off the Thursday rota for a month.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls WUB (cycle s4); partner: the old dog at the hospice window

== a letter to a daughter twenty years gone
tier: everyday
sphere: care
haunt: care.houses
ladder: regular
at: charity
rate: 0.5
share: .006
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 16-90
calls: WUB
holds: hospice volunteer
tone: mixed
life: community, family
horizon: week
roles: colleague
earth: a dying man asks you to write a letter to the daughter he has not spoken to in twenty years, and volunteers are told to keep out of family matters
times: Many hospice volunteers, once or twice in their years on the rota; the dying often want to reach a child they lost touch with (estimate)
gap: 1-3
scene: A man in the end bed asks {N} to write a letter for him, since his hands shake too much. It is to his daughter, whom he has not spoken to in twenty years. Volunteers are told to keep out of family matters.
scene W: The training was clear: volunteers listen, and leave family matters to the social worker.
scene U: {N} wonders what happened twenty years ago, and whether the daughter even knows he is ill.
scene B: Writing it makes {N} part of a family quarrel. Saying no keeps {Ns} place on the rota safe.
scene R: He has a few weeks at most. If he wants it written, it should be written tonight.
scene G: {N} thinks of the families who sit together here through the night, and of the empty chair by his bed.
- W | ask the social worker to help him write it, as the rules say | v: conformity, benevolence | sphere: care.W | chance: 75
- U | listen to his whole story first, then help him find the words | v: benevolence, universalism | sphere: care.U | chance: 75
- B | write it word for word as he says it, and leave the posting to him | v: security, benevolence | sphere: care.B | chance: 75
- R | write it with him tonight and post it on your way home | act: write it with him tonight and post it on their way home | v: benevolence, stimulation | sphere: care.R | chance: 75
- G | ask whether there is anyone else in the family he would want told | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: care.G | chance: 75
- W>G | tell the nurse in charge, and ask whether the hospice can reach his family | v: conformity, benevolence | sphere: care.W | chance: 65
- U>W | help him write only what is true, and leave the blame out of it | v: universalism | sphere: care.U | chance: 65
- B>U | write it on the hospice's paper, signed by him, so no one can say you meddled | act: write it on the hospice's paper, signed by him, so no one can say they meddled | v: security | sphere: care.B | chance: 65
- R>B | find the daughter online that evening and send the letter on yourself | act: find the daughter online that evening and send the letter on themselves | v: stimulation, self-direction | tech: internet | sphere: care.R | chance: 65
- G>R | read him back his own words slowly, and let him weep if he needs to | v: benevolence | sphere: care.G | chance: 65
works: A fortnight later a woman of forty sits in the chair by his bed, holding his hand.
works: The letter is posted, and he sleeps better than he has all month.
fails: No answer comes, and {N} sits with him through his last week, wondering if it ever reached her.
fails: The daughter rings the hospice, angry that a stranger wrote to her, and {N} is asked to explain.

# ================================================================ teaching assistant (learn.W)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls WU (cycle s1); partner: a helper's pay for a teacher's week

== the quiet copier in the reading group
tier: everyday
sphere: learn
ladder: newcomer
at: school
rate: 0.5
share: .02
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 17-70
calls: WU
holds: teaching assistant
tone: mixed
life: work
horizon: week
roles: colleague, boss
earth: a quiet girl in your reading group copies every word from her neighbour's book, and you begin to think she cannot see the board
times: Most teaching assistants, a few times in their years in class; poor sight in young children often goes unnoticed until an adult at school spots it (estimate)
gap: 0.5-2
scene: In {Ns} reading group, a quiet girl of seven copies every word from her neighbour's book and screws up her eyes at the board. She never asks for help. {N} begins to wonder whether she can see it at all.
scene W: Every child in the room should be able to see the lesson. Noticing the ones who cannot is {Ns} job.
scene U: {N} tries it quietly: the girl reads the big words on the wall, but not the small ones on the board.
scene B: The class teacher is busy and does not like being told things by the helper. A wrong guess would look bad.
scene R: {N} wants to sit her in the front row today and see what happens.
scene G: Her grandmother collects her at the gate every afternoon. She would want to know.
- W | tell the class teacher what you have seen, and ask for an eye check | act: tell the class teacher what they have seen, and ask for an eye check | v: benevolence, conformity | lever: voice | sphere: learn.W | chance: 75
- U | test it gently with big letters and small, front row and back | v: achievement, benevolence | sphere: learn.U | chance: 75
- B | mention it to the head in passing, so it is on record who spotted it | v: achievement, power | sphere: learn.B | chance: 75
- R | move her to the front row this morning, without waiting to ask | v: benevolence, self-direction | sphere: learn.R | chance: 75
- G | have a quiet word with her grandmother at the gate | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: learn.G | chance: 75
- W>U | fill in the school's form for the visiting nurse to check her eyes | v: conformity, benevolence | sphere: learn.W | chance: 65
- U>B | keep a week of notes on what she misses, so your word carries | act: keep a week of notes on what she misses, so their word carries | v: achievement, security | sphere: learn.U | chance: 65
- B>R | make her the board monitor, so she stands up close without anyone noticing | v: benevolence, achievement | sphere: learn.B | chance: 65
- R>G | read the board aloud for the whole group, so no one stands out | v: benevolence, universalism | sphere: learn.R | chance: 65
- G>W | ask the older staff how the school used to check every child's eyes | v: tradition, universalism | sphere: learn.G | chance: 65
works: Two weeks later she comes in wearing new glasses and reads the board aloud before anyone else.
works: The class teacher thanks {N} at the staff room door, and asks for the helper's eye on the whole class.
fails: The class teacher says the girl is just slow, and nothing is done until the spring.
fails: Her grandmother takes offence at the gate, and for a week the girl will not sit near {N}.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls BRG (cycle s2); partner: the quiet copier in the reading group

== a helper's pay for a teacher's week
tier: everyday
sphere: learn
ladder: newcomer
at: school
rate: 0.5
share: .02
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 17-70
calls: BRG
holds: teaching assistant
tone: trouble
life: work, money
horizon: week
roles: boss, colleague
earth: the class teacher is off sick, there is no money for cover, and you are asked to teach the whole class all week on a helper's pay
times: Many teaching assistants, a few times a year in short-staffed schools; assistants covering whole classes is a common complaint where cover budgets are tight (estimate)
gap: 0.5-2
scene: The class teacher is off sick for a week, and the school has no money for cover. {boss} asks {N} to take the whole class, lessons and all, on a helper's pay.
scene W: Thirty children deserve a proper teacher, and {N} is not one. Yet someone must stand at the front.
scene U: {N} has watched this class all year and knows which lessons work. A week could be done well.
scene B: A week in charge would look good on a training application. It also saves the school a teacher's wage.
scene R: Thirty eight-year-olds and no plans left by the teacher: {N} is half terrified and half thrilled.
scene G: The class trusts {N} already. A stranger at the front would unsettle them more.
- W | agree, but ask for the cover arrangement in writing | v: conformity, security | sphere: learn.W | chance: 75
- U | say yes, and plan the week around what the class already knows | v: achievement | sphere: learn.U | chance: 75
- B | say yes for a teacher's daily rate, or not at all | v: power, achievement | sphere: learn.B | chance: 75
- R | take the class and swap the set lessons for a week of projects | v: stimulation, self-direction | sphere: learn.R | chance: 75
- G | keep the class's days exactly as their own teacher runs them | v: tradition, security | sphere: learn.G | chance: 75
- W>B | agree, and ask that the week count towards your teacher training | act: agree, and ask that the week count towards their teacher training | v: achievement, conformity | sphere: learn.W | chance: 65
- U>R | plan the week so tightly that Friday afternoon is free for the class to choose | v: achievement, stimulation | sphere: learn.U | chance: 65
- B>G | say yes in return for a lasting post, so the class keeps a familiar face | v: security, tradition | sphere: learn.B | chance: 65
- R>W | refuse outright, and tell the head the children are owed a real teacher | v: universalism, self-direction | lever: voice | sphere: learn.R | chance: 65
- G>U | ring the retired teacher who taught this year group for decades, and ask her advice | v: tradition, achievement | sphere: learn.G | chance: 65
works: The week goes well, and on Friday the class gives {N} a card signed by all thirty.
works: {boss} finds money for cover after all, and the helpers are not asked again that year.
fails: The week is chaos by Wednesday, and {N} goes home each night too tired to eat.
fails: {boss} calls the helper difficult, and {Ns} hours are cut the next term.

# ================================================================ consultant (learn.B)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls UB (cycle s3); partner: extra days on the charity's invoice

== the report the client has already written
tier: everyday
sphere: learn
ladder: known
at: employer
rate: 0.5
share: .006
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 23-75
calls: UB
holds: consultant
tone: trouble
life: work, money
horizon: months
roles: boss, colleague
earth: a client pays for a review of its offices, has already decided to close half of them, and wants your report to say so
times: Many consultants, once or twice in their working years; a client wanting advice that backs a decision already taken is a well-known strain of advisory work (estimate)
gap: 1-3
scene: A firm has paid for {N} to review its twelve offices. On the second day its director makes clear that six will close whatever the review finds, and the report should say so.
scene W: A report with {Ns} name on it should say what the figures show, not what was ordered.
scene U: The figures say something else: four offices lose money, and two of the six make the most.
scene B: The director's firm is {Ns} biggest client this year, and it hires again only those who please.
scene R: {N} wants to tell the director, there in the meeting, that the fee could have been saved.
scene G: Two of the six offices are in small towns where the firm is the biggest employer for miles.
- W | write the report the figures support, and sign only that | v: universalism, conformity | sphere: learn.W | chance: 75
- U | lay the figures for all twelve offices side by side, and let them argue | v: achievement, universalism | sphere: learn.U | chance: 75
- B | give the director the report that was wanted, and send the invoice on time | v: achievement, security | closed: approval: advice bent to fit what a client wants; backfire: the closures go badly and the report is quoted | sphere: learn.B | chance: 75
- R | tell the director to their face that the review is a sham | v: self-direction | mark: made an enemy | sphere: learn.R | chance: 75
- G | visit the two small-town offices before writing a word | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: learn.G | chance: 75
- W>R | write the honest report, and give up the account if it is refused | v: universalism, self-direction | lever: exit | mark: turned down a chance | sphere: learn.W | chance: 65
- U>G | work out what closing the two small-town offices would cost those towns | v: universalism, benevolence | sphere: learn.U | chance: 65
- B>W | agree to six closures, but trade the two best offices for the four that lose money | v: power, universalism | sphere: learn.B | chance: 65
- R>U | spend a night running every figure again until you are sure who is right | act: spend a night running every figure again until they are sure who is right | v: achievement, stimulation | sphere: learn.R | chance: 65
- G>B | ask your old mentor in the trade how to keep both the client and your name | act: ask their old mentor in the trade how to keep both the client and their name | v: tradition, security | sphere: learn.G | chance: 65
works: The director reads the figures, swears, and closes four offices instead of six.
works: The report is honest, and other firms start asking for {N} by name.
fails: The client takes the work to a firm that writes what it is told, and the year's income halves.
fails: The six offices close anyway, and {Ns} name is on the report the papers quote.

