== the car no one makes parts for
tier: everyday
sphere: learn
haunt: prod.craft
ladder: known
at: employer
rate: 0.5
share: .005
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 16-75
calls: UR
holds: mechanic
tone: mixed
life: work
horizon: months
roles: boss, colleague
earth: a widow wants her late husband's old car kept running, and the part it needs has not been made for years
times: Many mechanics, once or twice in their years at a small garage; old cars outliving their parts are a familiar job there (estimate)
gap: 1-5
scene: A widow brings in the car her husband kept for forty years. It needs a fuel pump that has not been made for decades, and {boss} says to tell her the car is finished.
scene W: She deserves a straight price and an honest answer, the same as any customer.
scene U: {N} has the old pump on the bench in pieces. Only one small part has worn through.
scene B: A job like this takes days and pays for hours. The other jobs on the board pay better.
scene R: {N} wants to make the part from scratch on the lathe, just to see if it can be done.
